    "title": "Flagger working in construction zone of US-33 hit, killed by car - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Megan Finke ,\n8 hours ago Oliver Helbig/Getty Images By Oliver Helbig A flagger working in a construction zone in Auglaize County was hit and killed by a car on Wednesday, according to an Ohio State Highway Patrol spokesperson.\n[DOWNLOAD: Free WHIO-TV News app for alerts as news breaks ]\nThe crash happened on US 33 just east of State Route 65 south in Clay Township.\nTRENDING STORIES:\nA preliminary investigation found that a 35-year-old man was driving a 2021 Jeep Grand Cherokee east on US-33 when he struck the worker.\nThe victim has been identified as Troy Ray, 58, of Clyde, Ohio.\nHe was working as a flagger in a construction zone in the eastbound lane.\nThe driver of the Jeep was not injured in this crash.\nJoseph was wearing his seatbelt and did not sustain any injuries.\nTroopers do not believe alcohol or drugs contributed to this crash.\nThe crash remains under investigation by the Wapakoneta Post of the Ohio State Highway Patrol.\n[SIGN UP: WHIO-TV Daily Headlines Newsletter ]\n2",
    "summary": "8 hours ago Oliver Helbig/Getty Images By Oliver Helbig A flagger working in a construction zone in Auglaize County was hit and killed by a car on Wednesday, according to an Ohio State Highway Patrol spokesperson. [DOWNLOAD: Free WHIO-TV News app for alerts as news breaks ] The crash happened on US 33 just east of State Route 65 south in Clay Township. A preliminary investigation found that a 35-year-old man was driving a 2021 Jeep Grand Cherokee east on US-33 when he struck the worker. He was working as a flagger in a construction zone in the eastbound lane.",
